{#
  The held-action card: the clearest expression of "the model proposes, code
  decides".

  This is the single most important partial in the kit. Every side-effect action
  can be held, so every app with agents needs somewhere for the owner to decide —
  and an app without one has agents that pause invisibly, which the owner
  discovers only when they wonder why nothing happened.

  It renders what the auditor actually produced, not a summary of it:
    hold.owner_question  what the owner must decide, in plain language
    hold.findings        which rule(s) held it, and why
    hold.arguments       the proposed call, with sensitive keys masked
    hold.tool            which tool would run

  Approve and Decline post with HTMX so the decision does not reload the page and
  lose the rest of the queue. Both carry the hold_id, because an approval applies
  only to the exact action that was held.

  Fields come from audit_agent.contracts.HoldRecord: hold_id, request_id, app_id,
  agent_id, principal, task_type, tool, arguments, findings, owner_question,
  created_at, status. A missing one renders as an empty cell rather than a broken
  page, because the queue must stay usable when the runtime is mid-upgrade.
#}
{% set hold = hold | default({}) %}
{#-
  Every field is normalised here rather than defaulted inline, because under
  StrictUndefined `{% if hold.status %}` RAISES when the key is absent — only the
  `default` filter is safe, since it receives the Undefined without touching it.
  A hold mid-write, or one from an older runtime, must still render: the queue is
  the owner's view of what is paused, and a page that errors hides every other
  pending action behind it.
-#}
{% set hold_id = hold.hold_id | default('') %}
{% set hold_tool = hold.tool | default('') %}
{% set hold_status = hold.status | default('') %}
{% set hold_task = hold.task_type | default('') %}
{% set hold_agent = hold.agent_id | default('') %}
{% set hold_created = hold.created_at | default('') %}
{% set hold_decided_by = hold.decided_by | default('') %}
{% set hold_decided_at = hold.decided_at | default('') %}
{% set decide_url = decide_url | default('holds/decide') %}
<article class="held" id="hold-{{ hold_id or 'unknown' }}">
  <div class="held__head">
    <span class="held__tool">{{ hold_tool or '(unknown tool)' }}</span>
    {% if hold_status %}
      <span class="badge badge--{{ 'ok' if hold_status == 'approved' else ('danger' if hold_status == 'rejected' else 'hold') }}">{{ hold_status }}</span>
    {% else %}
      <span class="badge badge--hold">awaiting your decision</span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  {# The question is what the owner reads first. `default(..., true)` is required:
     without the boolean second argument an EMPTY string is not treated as missing,
     so a hold whose owner_question is blank would render nothing to decide on.
     Falls back to the rule messages rather than leaving the owner guessing. #}
  <p class="held__question">
    {{ hold.owner_question | default('An action needs your approval before it runs.', true) }}
  </p>

  {% set findings = hold.findings | default([]) %}
  {% if findings %}
    <div class="held__reason">
      {% for finding in findings %}
        {% set severity = finding.severity | default('') %}
        <p class="mt-0">
          <span class="held__rule">{{ finding.rule_id | default('rule') }}</span>
          {%- if severity %} <span class="badge badge--{{ severity }}">{{ severity }}</span>{% endif %}
          <br>{{ finding.message | default('') }}
        </p>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% set args = (hold.arguments | default({})) | mask %}
  {% if args %}
    <table class="args">
      <caption class="sr-only">Proposed arguments</caption>
      <tbody>
        {% for key, value in args.items() | sort %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{{ key }}</th>
            {# A masked value gets its own styling so the owner can see that
               something was withheld deliberately, rather than assuming the field
               is empty. #}
            <td class="{{ 'masked' if value == '***REDACTED***' else '' }}">{{ value }}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  {% else %}
    <p class="tiny muted">This action carries no arguments.</p>
  {% endif %}

  {# Decisions are scoped to the exact held action, so the hold_id travels with
     the request and the server compares the proposed arguments before executing.
     An approval that applied to "the next thing this agent does" would be a
     standing permission, which is not what a hold is. #}
  {% if hold_status in ('', 'pending') %}
    <form class="btn-row" method="post"
          hx-post="{{ decide_url }}"
          hx-target="#hold-{{ hold_id or 'unknown' }}"
          hx-swap="outerHTML">
      <input type="hidden" name="hold_id" value="{{ hold_id }}">
      <button class="btn btn--ok" type="submit" name="decision" value="approve">Approve</button>
      <button class="btn btn--danger" type="submit" name="decision" value="decline">Decline</button>
      <span class="htmx-indicator tiny muted" aria-live="polite">working…</span>
    </form>
  {% else %}
    <p class="held__meta">
      Decided {{ hold_decided_at or '—' }}
      {% if hold_decided_by %} by {{ hold_decided_by }}{% endif %}.
    </p>
  {% endif %}

  <p class="held__meta">
    hold <span class="mono">{{ hold_id or '—' }}</span>
    · task <span class="mono">{{ hold_task or '—' }}</span>
    · agent <span class="mono">{{ hold_agent or '—' }}</span>
    · raised {{ hold_created or '—' }}
  </p>
</article>
